  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Dal baati churma is a trio: baked wheat rounds called "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "baati ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "baati"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", a sweetened wheat crumble called "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "churma ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "churma"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", and a spiced five-lentil broth called "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "panchmel dal ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "panchmel-dal"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Each element is made separately and brought together at the table."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The baati dough should be stiff, not soft. Use minimal water. A soft dough will spread and not hold its round shape during baking."
          }
        ]
      },
